hr/rec-harness/artifacts/unirank-taobao-macro-12h-20261109T043023Z\", \"data_identity\": \"9f110bfc2f037f36e2f48787b812df640fe5df2de1cda8db7ac04590c1c9be44\", \"dataset_revision\": \"fd01fb8edbfa58bb4b0d6556f1d5838074b0dbe5\", \"epochs\": 1, \"batch_size\": 8192, \"history_limit\": 100, \"train_seed\": 20262027, \"num_workers\": 0, \"tasks\": [\"is_click\", \"cart\", \"fav\", \"buy\"], \"primary\": \"four-task macro ROC-AUC\", \"selection_policy\": {\"id\": \"taobao-four-task-macro-auc-v1\", \"split\": \"validation\", \"tasks\": [\"is_click\", \"cart\", \"fav\", \"buy\"], \"weights\": {\"is_click\": 0.25, \"cart\": 0.25, \"fav\": 0.25, \"buy\": 0.25}, \"primary\": \"macro_auc\", \"direction\": \"maximize\", \"tie_breakers\": [\"macro_logloss ascending\", \"parameters ascending\", \"trial_id ascending\"], \"missing_task\": \"invalid; never average only the available tasks\", \"regression_policy\": \"Report each task's AUC and Logloss change against the reference and entry model; explain trade-offs in topic decisions. No undeclared per-task veto threshold.\", \"test_policy\": \"Selection uses validation only; freeze before a single held-out assessment. Historical completed test suites remain unchanged.\"}, \"secondary\": \"Macro Logloss; every task AUC/Logloss and per-task deltas; measured model and runtime cost\", \"dense_optimizer\": \"AdamW\", \"dense_learning_rate\": 0.0001, \"sparse_optimizer\": \"Adagrad\", \"sparse_learning_rate\": 0.05, \"gradient_clip\": 10.0, \"gradient_clip_scope\": \"dense parameters only, following upstream split optimizer training\", \"precision\": \"bf16 autocast; TF32 disabled; no torch.compile\", \"history_policy\": \"official_offline\", \"history_visibility\": \"Exact released prefix/action inputs. Delayed feedback may not be mature at prediction time; results only establish this offline benchmark.\", \"drop_last\": {\"train\": true, \"valid\": false}, \"full_validation_samples\": 2871767, \"training\": \"scratch; official single-pass recipe adapted to DIN; sum four BCE unless declared training-loss hook\", \"baseline\": \"Initial empirical reference: DIN local activation over item-field history with action values and four separate heads; field/task adaptation, not exact original DIN reproduction\", \"research_goal\": \"Explore and validate mechanism-distinct unified modeling of multi-field user/context/target features and multi-feedback behavior histories. Develop representations and information flow that jointly support sequence modeling, feature interaction and task prediction under the fixed data and compute protocol.\", \"architecture_search\": {\"scope\": \"Whole-model design, including replacement of the initial network and all internal representations.\", \"design_dimensions\": [\"Representation units: fields, events, behavior groups, learned slots and target/task tokens.\", \"Information flow: stacked interaction, layer-wise joint interaction, parallel exchange, learned routing or other testable unified structures.\", \"History selection/compression jointly designed with target/context-conditioned retrieval.\", \"Derived features computed from authorized inputs: field matches, behavior counts/composition, grouping and sequence positions.\", \"Shared and task-conditioned representations, prediction readouts and registered training-loss mechanisms.\"], \"lineage\": \"parent_trial identifies a comparison and evidence lineage; it does not require code or architectural inheritance. inherited_components may be empty when the whole model is replaced.\", \"proposal_unit\": \"A coherent mechanism hypothesis can require several coordinated structural changes. Build that structure and plan component, replacement or factorial controls to identify where its value comes from.\", \"evidence\": \"Select by the equal-weight validation AUC mean across click, cart, favorite and purchase; report macro Logloss and every task change. Use that same rule for checkpoints, parents, topic gains, merge eligibility and final selection. Evaluate mechanism support, nearest-work differences and measured cost; compare closest architectural alternatives and the initial reference.\", \"fixed_contracts\": \"Available sample information, labels, data split, scoring, resource accounting and the frozen host training recipe remain shared. Internal architecture and readout design are candidate choices.\", \"reference_use\": \"UniRank comparison methods provide inspectable design references and nearest work. Agents choose and adapt mechanisms from local evidence.\"}, \"research_budget\": {\"seconds\": 43200, \"start_event\": \"new_campaign_started_with_verified_dataset\", \"start_unix\": 1794198624.5008233, \"deadline_unix\": 1794241824.5008233}, \"test_policy\": \"closed during research; any final suite must be frozen before held-out scoring\", \"source_sha256\": {\"baseline.py\": \"f4b473cbacf60d72cff90f3721ad754dd617ee6065fe3fca2fc9cd4be2b25c36\", \"train.py\": \"a313f015c9d03ae8244861bc36ff58517d8b630b968c397f404f627ea631522e\", \"visibility.py\": \"d1f641c62fa3c72e1eadc03aad6d999cc9af87fceb783775eb22d1405d9ac6b4\", \"data.py\": \"ef28cb65880b6931d3e567d2bfb4a67d7530c18067b68e47bf483b65b2560438\", \"selection.py\": \"aa519982aebe726806e1d11b68fca2574d33993778c3392997843fe489fd9aff\", \"selection-policy.json\": \"8e568c065a0412009879a3d42569e3469df6e6b81fb2837f94a1e04d39ffacf4\"}, \"upstream_commit\": \"90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\", \"benchmark_deviations\": [\"DIN is the initial empirical reference; unified research candidates can use entirely different architectures.\", \"One GPU per model; batch8192 per model (single-device rather than published distributed global batch).\", \"Validation selection uses the arithmetic mean of all four task AUCs; all tasks are reported separately.\", \"Validation includes every sample; upstream default drop_last may omit remainders.\", \"In-process DataLoader (num_workers=0): container shared memory is512MiB; all compared runs use the same loading policy.\", \"No torch.compile; BF16; TF32 disabled.\"], \"trial_cap_seconds\": 1208.5413760878146, \"estimated_unit_seconds\": 483.4165504351258, \"estimated_validation_seconds\": 75.56942507252097, \"frozen_unix\": 1794198639.34825, \"identity\": \"427fc51900560816321ba9bbc170639eb26625972df75b22e3c47d523c363748\"}\nmethod \"auto\"\nbudget_scope \"The research wall clock starts at protocol.research_budget.start_unix under its recorded start_event. Original acquisition uses verified download completion; an explicitly requested rerun on already verified data has its own fixed campaign start. Every later preparation step, calibration, agent call, failure, training/control and scoring job counts.\"\nno_test_feedback true\nknowledge_revision \"knowledge-access-v3\"\nknowledge_review {\"policy\": \"Evaluate relevant external references against local evidence; adoption is optional. Missing source detail and negative transfer remain explicit.\", \"proposal_output\": \"Add top-level knowledge_assessments: [{knowledge_id, decision: used|considered|rejected|unresolved, rationale, transformed_mechanism, variant_names, nearest_work_difference, falsifier}]. Cover retrieved industry cards; identify the concrete changed mechanism for used cards. This is provenance, not causal proof.\", \"reflection\": \"Review the latest knowledge-usage.json alongside outcomes; distinguish declared use, executed changes, mechanism evidence and unresolved attribution.\"}\nlatest_knowledge_usage {\"revision\": \"knowledge-access-v3\", \"retrieved_ids\": [\"unirank-method-infnet\", \"unirank-method-onetrans\", \"unirank-method-ultrahstu\"], \"assessments\": [{\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-infnet\", \"decision\": \"used\", \"rationale\": \"Pinned benchmark aggregation/broadcast source inspected as nearest work. Its task-aware multi-view aggregation motivates the controlled read of retained g0 structured state; this is external design provenance, not local effectiveness evidence. Previous declared use produced no supported match-prior gain; revise that explanation rather than erase the null result. Original paper detail remains unaudited.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"Reuse existing four task queries and tied Q/K/V to read final g0 field/relation tokens at both query-refinement stages; retain one-way exact masks, no global-to-local broadcast, unchanged raw-event terminal pool. Uniform active addressing controls the proposed query dependence.\", \"variant_names\": [\"state_adaptive_none\", \"state_uniform_none\", \"state_adaptive_prior\", \"state_uniform_prior\"], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"No new hubs, separate group fusion or affine gated broadcasts. Parameter-neutral memory substitution within the imported hybrid, with an explicit routing-by-prior factorial and strictly masked state keys.\", \"falsifier\": \"No gain beyond current hybrid_none and source bests, gains matched by uniform addressing, or cost/seed effects explaining the gain oppose this tested utility claim.\", \"source_refs\": [\"unirank-benchmark-v2\", \"unirank-code:INFNet\", \"paper:infnet\"], \"executed_refs\": [{\"trial_id\": \"g1-r0007-state_adaptive_none\", \"source_sha256\": \"8c6c3db4a7a6549da72e3f232a677858fb5d2fbf5e8073caf605ca59861ed9b7\", \"status\": \"success\"}, {\"trial_id\": \"g1-r0007-state_uniform_none\", \"source_sha256\": \"7450050efa2875c3a9f08fa0d3af41cb65eb9c81b8c747975ea0caa1ab07a254\", \"status\": \"success\"}, {\"trial_id\": \"g1-r0007-state_adaptive_prior\", \"source_sha256\": \"aa95422c0ddce0f348661f987f822cf6cd8a210c6b66da73eec72ea968bb5820\", \"status\": \"success\"}, {\"trial_id\": \"g1-r0007-state_uniform_prior\", \"source_sha256\": \"2d32aaf1b938ed33f7a84f6d775afa9a090047257c12e4414d817f4262f86984\", \"status\": \"success\"}], \"evidence_class\": \"agent-declared usage; not mechanism confirmation\"}, {\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-ultrahstu\", \"decision\": \"considered\", \"rationale\": \"Retrieved card documents hybrid sparse/full sequence transduction; no original-paper audit or local support is available. Full sequence updates are not needed for the observed mean-seed/refinement limitation and would confound this bounded memory substitution.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"None; no HSTU transduction, sparsity pattern or active-sequence truncation adopted.\", \"variant_names\": [], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"Fixed100-event visibility; read-only g0 token memory for four queries, original events only for final pooling. No comparative claim against UltraHSTU.\", \"falsifier\": \"A later primary audit and matched-cost experiment showing useful event-state updates would reopen this option; this study cannot refute that architecture.\", \"source_refs\": [\"unirank-benchmark-v2\", \"unirank-code:UltraHSTU\", \"paper:ultrahstu\"], \"executed_refs\": [], \"evidence_class\": \"agent-declared usage; not mechanism confirmation\"}, {\"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-onetrans\", \"decision\": \"considered\", \"rationale\": \"The inherited latest_knowledge_usage record considered the pinned mixed sequence/nonsequence implementation and progressive reduction. This turn does not independently re-audit that source or adopt its full-stream updates; its effectiveness remains an external report. The current follow-up is driven by the observed hybrid null prior results and inspected local source.\", \"transformed_mechanism\": \"None newly adopted from this card. Keep the fixed visible prefix and four-query read-only branch; substitute g0 structured state for narrow-read memory.\", \"variant_names\": [], \"nearest_work_difference\": \"No progressive sequence pruning or whole-stream replacement. No assertion of equivalence or superiority to original OneTrans; inherited source inspection is provenance only.\", \"falsifier\": \"A later primary audit and matched-cost stream-update control could reveal missing information in this read-only structure; current experiments cannot refute that alternative.\", \"source_refs