{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast, hashlib, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/workspace');r=json.load(open('/tmp/runtime_r001.json'));ctx=r['context'];hist={t['id']:t for t in ctx['history']};parent=ctx['incumbent']\ndef cfg(f):\n t=ast.parse((p/f).read_text());return ast.literal_eval(next(n.value for n in t.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(v,ast.Name) and v.id=='CONFIG' for v in n.targets)))\nshared=['Frozen protocol '+r['required_study_protocol_ref'], 'Released input and label identities, temporal split, task masks and 100-event visibility', 'One full training pass, batch 8192, train seed 20262027, optimizer, precision, clipping and host BCE loss', 'All g0 representations, feedback memory, JointBlock, raw static and pooled features, four original task towers', 'Same parameter shapes, initialization ordering, zero-start residual output, and no terminal match prior', 'No model I/O, external inputs, test access, or candidate training-loss hook']\ncontrast=lambda intervention,control,confounds,supported,unsupported:{'parent_ref':parent,'intervention':intervention,'control':control,'held_fixed':shared,'remaining_confounds':confounds,'decision_if_supported':supported,'decision_if_not_supported':unsupported}\nstudy={\n'id':'g1-t001-r0008-retrieval-replacements',\n'protocol_ref':r['required_study_protocol_ref'],\n'evidence_refs':ctx['allowed_observation_ids'],\n'question':\\\"Does the hybrid's small validation advantage require g0 token content in event-addressing queries or learned terminal event weights, or can an active low-rank residual on a simple historical mean or the inherited DIN sum reproduce it? The current incumbent g1-r0007-state_uniform_none scores 0.8307177422018418 versus g0's 0.8301982212762624, but costs 947.02 versus 443.35 training seconds; its purchase AUC is lower by 0.00167493 and click AUC by 0.00018044. These single-seed results motivate attribution before adding another mechanism.\\\",\n'hypothesis':\\\"The remaining learned terminal event-addressing operation may provide complementary history information after uniform reading of g0 state. If its advantage specifically comes from compatibility with g0 representation content, intact-state adaptive pooling should beat the identity-state adaptive replacement. If learned event selection matters, it should also beat masked-mean pooling. Conversely, mean or DIN replacements matching or exceeding the intact hybrid would favor simpler summary/optimization explanations for this tested gain. This is a discriminating replacement study; no new general attention mechanism, novelty, additivity of source gains, or expected performance improvement is asserted.\\\",\n'nearest_work':[\n {'source_ref':'trial://g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Inherit its complete field/relation/position and feedback representation, shared JointBlock and original towers. The hybrid adds a zero-start transformed wide historical summary. This study changes only what feeds that residual branch, retaining g0 tower inputs.'},\n {'source_ref':'trial://g1-r0007-state_uniform_none','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Exact source is replayed byte-for-byte. New arms replace terminal event weights or token content used only by the residual branch; all modules, shapes, loss and initialization remain inherited.'},\n {'source_ref':'trial://g1-r0004-match_terminal_only','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'The source uses evolving feature queries and target-match addressing. The tested hybrid retains task queries and a wide raw-value read after g0 interaction. Terminal match priors remain disabled following local negative transfer.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived primary text lines 271-277 explains retaining unnormalized interest intensity. The DIN residual control transforms the inherited signed sum rather than introducing a second normalized event summary; it is not an exact DIN reproduction.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:hyformer https://arxiv.org/html/2601.12681v1 sections 3.3-3.5; unirank-code:HyFormer lines 221-243','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Primary paper uses global feature-derived queries, sequence decoding and query boosting; pinned benchmark forward inspected separately. Here g0 tokens remain read-only, followed by a single wide event summary. No HyFormer sequence encoder or boosting implementation is adopted.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:hemix https://arxiv.org/html/2602.09387v1 sections 3.1-3.3; unirank-code:HeMix lines 215-237','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Primary paper describes fixed and feature-conditioned interest queries and heterogeneous mixing. Identity-state replacement supplies a local fixed/task-and-occupancy query control; no global versus real-time sequence split or HeteroMixer is imported.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:mixformer https://arxiv.org/html/2602.14110v1 section 3.3; unirank-code:MixFormer lines 187-218','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Primary paper alternates feature-query mixing, sequence attention and fusion. This study neither co-updates event tokens nor adopts its mixer. It tests whether content-conditioned terminal selection is necessary in this existing hybrid.'}\n],\n'inherited_components':['All g0 model code except adding the already committed hybrid branch call; 25 incumbent methods unchanged in new modules', 'Existing task identities, two narrow task mixers, Q/K/V maps, raw event projection and rank embeddings', 'Original 112-to-32-to-112 bias-free maps, nonaffine LayerNorm and zero-start 112-to-112 residual output at default dimensions', 'Exact masking, null handling, current-action sanitization and frozen four-task sum-BCE host training', 'Incumbent uniform structured-state reads, disabled terminal prior, same module construction/RNG isolation and all original prediction towers'],\n'proposed_difference':\\\"Submit one masked-mean residual candidate and three controls. mean_residual supplies a convex uniform mean of valid raw historical values to the existing low-rank normalized residual. identity_attention replaces only the branch's final g0 tokens with existing learned token identities, preserving the exact token-valid mask, seed/refinement structure, task identities and adaptive event weights; intact g0 tokens still enter every prediction tower. din_reparameterization supplies the already computed global signed DIN sum to the same residual transformation, with no second learned selection. incumbent_replay is the exact committed source. In replacement modules adaptive event scores, narrow reads and match computations remain executed, so this is attribution before pruning. No uniform-by-identity fourth factorial cell is trained: when terminal weights are uniform, queries cannot affect the value summary, making that cell structurally redundant.\\\",\n'predictions':[\n 'If g0 state content contributes specifically through the new event-addressing branch, incumbent_replay should exceed identity_attention on validation macro AUC under the same seed and host recipe. Otherwise the tested content-conditioned compatibility hypothesis lacks support.',\n 'If learned terminal selection contributes beyond a simple extra mean-history channel, incumbent_replay should exceed mean_residual. Similar performance would favor removal of adaptive retrieval in a later pruned, measured implementation.',\n 'If additional residual parameterization of information already available to the tower explains the gain, din_reparameterization should reproduce the improvement over g0 and approach the incumbent. Mean outperforming DIN would instead motivate a narrower normalized/raw-summary hypothesis; that contrast alone does not isolate normalization from weighting.',\n 'Identity-adaptive queries retain task identity and temporal-bin presence, so they may still exploit generic task/history preference through event keys. They are not sample-information-free queries.',\n 'Report macro AUC and Logloss, all four task deltas against DIN, g0, the g1 source and incumbent. History slices remain empty, 1-16, 17-64, >64 with counts; no slice selects checkpoints. Empty-history predictions within trained arms can differ through shared training even though branch outputs are forced to zero for empty histories.'\n],\n'falsifiers':[\n 'An identity-only branch matching or beating the intact incumbent opposes the claim that per-sample g0 state content is necessary for this branch under the tested protocol.',\n 'A uniform mean matching or beating the intact incumbent opposes a learned-terminal-weight explanation of the observed hybrid gain.',\n 'A DIN reparameterization matching the hybrid and beating g0 weakens a complementary-retrieval explanation and favors added residual capacity or optimization. No single-seed near-tie is called equivalence or significance.',\n 'Failure to exceed g0 on repetitions, or unexplained replay/parity discrepancies, prevents a repeatable added-utility conclusion. A failed numerical preflight is an implementation failure, not scientific counterevidence.'\n],\n'alternative_explanations':[\n 'One-seed checkpoint selection, sampling variation, and cumulative validation selection can account for the small gain; repeated seeds do not identify a mechanism.',\n 'Added low-rank residual capacity, output normalization, optimization conditioning, shared embedding gradients or branch-specific backward paths can explain gains without representation-interaction complementarity.',\n 'Equal nominal parameters do not imply equal expressive capacity: uniform and DIN replacements deactivate query dependence and share the residual summary across tasks; identity replacement retains occupancy information. Effective gradient-active capacity and measured backward cost must be reported.',\n 'DIN versus mean changes signed weights, aggregate scale, and target dependence together. This is a replacement control, not an isolated test of normalization or intensity; a future scale/weight factorial would be needed.',\n 'Single-pass training may favor one residual parameterization. Identical data passes support mechanism comparisons, not equal-compute efficiency claims.',\n 'Observed cart/favorite gains and purchase/click regressions can cancel in macro AUC; auxiliary labels are user/category/brand matches within 24h, not advertisement-specific conversions. Offline feedback visibility and vocabulary construction limit production transfer.'\n],\n'contrasts':[\n contrast('incumbent_replay: intact final g0 token content seeds and refines task queries before adaptive terminal pooling','identity_attention: replace branch tokens with the original learned token identities under the same token-valid mask', ['Token identity remains trainable and shared with the original g0 path; dynamic content and gradient coupling both change. This establishes necessity only for the tested content path.'], 'Retain content-conditioned addressing for repetition if validation improvement survives replay and resource checks.', 'Do not credit g0 content-conditioned query refinement; consider fixed task/occupancy queries and preserve the null finding.'),\n contrast('incumbent_replay: learned per-task terminal event weights','mean_residual: uniform weights over exactly the same valid events and zero null for empty histories', ['Query dependence and effective capacity are reduced; task summaries collapse to a common mean. Parameter shapes and nominal forward work are matched, effective backward work is not.'], 'Retain learned selection only if its gain justifies measured cost and survives repetition.', 'Treat masked mean as a simpler candidate; plan pruning only after attribution, with a fresh measured cost comparison.'),\n contrast('mean_residual: normalized raw-history mean as the residual source','din_reparameterization: inherited global signed DIN sum as the residual source; existing g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate is the no-extra-branch anchor', ['Target dependence, signed weights, magnitude and optimization change together; active value maps are equal but query maps are inactive. No scalar-normalization attribution is justified.'], 'If mean beats DIN and g0, provisionally retain a complementary mean-history channel; isolate the source of that gain in a later admissible study.', 'If DIN matches the hybrid, report residual-capacity/optimization as a viable alternative. If neither beats g0 on repeats, retain g0 as the cheaper supported source.'),\n contrast('incumbent_replay: exact source and configuration under frozen host seed','g1-r0007-state_uniform_none committed validation receipt and source hash', ['Historical environment or nondeterminism may affect equality. A reproducible source hash alone does not guarantee numeric parity.'], 'Use replay as the contemporaneous anchor and pair selected candidate/closest control in reserved validation repetitions.', 'Diagnose any discrepancy using host parity gates before interpreting mechanism contrasts; charge failed checks and do not automatically duplicate unknown jobs.')\n],\n'cost_plan':{\n 'estimate_ref':'g1-r0007-state_uniform_none: 1001.10 s full unit, 947.02 s train, 44.29 s inference, 33070309 parameters, 1277093 dense, 9631821824 peak GPU bytes; g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate: 490.25 s full unit. Runtime snapshot remaining_seconds=10868.616738319397; all preparation since that snapshot also counts.',\n 'all_variants_counted':True,\n 'attribution_reserve':'Four complete full-protocol units are requested, including exact replay and both active replacement controls: about 4004 s at historical cost; use 1250 s/unit, 5000 s total for admission. Same nominal 33070309 parameters predicted for every arm; host must measure and reject unexplained mismatch. No extra screening or local training. Include preflights, failures and scoring in ledger.',\n 'assessment_reserve':'Reserve approximately 4500 s for two additional host-authorized paired validation seeds of the selected model and closest surviving control (four units around 1000 s each plus diagnostics), targeting three seeds when feasible. Freeze that comparison before repetitions. This does not fund three seeds for all four arms plus both sources; g0 and the original g1 source remain single-seed references unless the live ledger permits their necessary repeats. Report omissions and keep comparisons to those sources preliminary. Test access is unavailable.',\n 'stop_rule':'Read the live host ledger before executing; do not enlarge the fixed 43200 s budget. Admit the four-arm suite only if estimated remaining cost including at least 4500 s repetition/diagnostic reserve fits after preparation. Reestimate from actual receipts; stop or reduce later repetitions if no complete admissible unit fits. No automatic retries of unknown-state jobs; all failed preflights and attempts count. Negative or inconclusive results satisfy faithful research reporting, not scientific success.'}\n}\nvariants=[]\nfor name,file,role,note in [\n ('mean_residual','candidate.py','candidate','Prospective masked-mean history residual, same nominal modules and common retrieval computations. No new measurements or efficiency claim.'),\n ('incumbent_replay','incumbent_replay.py','control','Exact byte-for-byte committed incumbent reproduction, including literal CONFIG. Contemporaneous comparison anchor; original receipt remains unchanged.'),\n ('identity_attention','identity_attention.py','control','Adaptive raw-event pooling with only learned token identities and validity supplied to query seeding/refinement. Original g0 tokens and original tower inputs stay intact.'),\n ('din_reparameterization','din_reparameterization.py','control','Active low-rank normalized residual of existing global signed DIN sum. No newly selected history information; common query/event computations retained with zero dependence.')]:\n sha=hashlib.sha256((p/file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n variants.append({'name':name,'file':file,'role':role,'config':cfg(file),'note':note+' Source SHA256 '+sha+'. Host numerical preflight is mandatory; no local torch or training available. Parameter count is inherited, not numerically measured for the new modules.'})\nknowledge=[]\nfor id,why,diff,falsifier in [\n ('unirank-method-hyformer','Considered as nearest query-decoding/query-boosting reference; primary paper sections 3.3-3.5 and pinned benchmark block inspected. Local evidence, rather than the card, motivates attribution.','No sequence encoder or query-boosting stack is adopted; existing g0 tokens remain read-only.','If removing g0 query content does not hurt, content-conditioned decoding is not supported here.'),\n ('unirank-method-hemix','Considered fixed versus feature-conditioned query alternatives; original methodology and pinned tokenizer inspected. Does not establish transfer to this data.','Identity-state control uses existing task/token identities under current masks, without HeMix multi-sequence tokenization or heterogeneous mixer.','Identity-only adaptive retrieval matching the incumbent weakens the need for a feature-conditioned query path.'),\n ('unirank-method-mixformer','Considered coupled feature-query and sequence interactions; primary section 3.3 and pinned forward inspected. No method effectiveness imported.','No sequence co-update or MixFormer QueryMixer is adopted; replacement tests target necessity of the already committed terminal retrieval.','Uniform mean or DIN residual matching the incumbent weakens a high-order content-driven retrieval explanation.')]:\n knowledge.append({'knowledge_id':id,'decision':'considered','rationale':why,'transformed_mechanism':'None adopted as a new architecture; used only to frame nearest-work distinctions and alternative explanations.','variant_names':[v['name'] for v in variants],'nearest_work_difference':diff,'falsifier':falsifier})\nreview=[]\nbase=hist['g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate'];inc=hist[parent]\nfor t in ctx['history']:\n val=t['validation'];review.append({'id':t['id'],'status':t['status'],'macro_auc':val['macro_auc'],'macro_logloss':val['macro_logloss'],'delta_auc_vs_g0':val['macro_auc']-base['validation']['macro_auc'],'parameters':t.get('parameters'),'train_seconds':t.get('train_seconds'),'inference_seconds':val['inference_seconds'],'wall_seconds':t['wall_seconds'],'interpretation':'Single-seed authorized validation observation; no test results inspected.'})\nproposal={\n 'study':study,'parent_trial':parent,'variants':variants,'knowledge_assessments':knowledge,\n 'evidence_review':{'maturity':'local_observation; controlled directional patterns at one seed, no repeated support','observations':review,'trajectory_interpretation':[\n 'Baseline DIN establishes the initial reference at 0.8099233881; g0 supplies a much stronger representation baseline at 0.8301982213.',\n 'Original g1 match-terminal source scores 0.8192325306, below g0. Its gains cannot be added to g0.',\n 'Round 6 hybrid with no prior beats its adaptive, uniform and rotated priors. Thus terminal match prior transfer was unsuccessful here; do not revive it without new evidence.',\n 'Round 7 state refinement beats event refinement modestly, but state adaptive does not beat state uniform, and either terminal-prior arm regresses. No learned structured-state routing advantage is established.',\n 'Incumbent deltas against g0 by task AUC are click -0.0001804354, cart +0.0014396873, favorite +0.0024937635, purchase -0.0016749316; corresponding Logloss deltas are -0.0000454662, -0.0001006790, -0.0000512033, +0.0000455380.',\n 'Incumbent slice macro deltas against g0: empty +0.00840937 (6444 samples; only 13 purchase positives), 1-16 +0.00043211 (461684), 17-64 +0.00132917 (1001754), >64 -0.00007266 (1401885). Empty-history branch output is forced zero, so that slice gain is not direct retrieval evidence.',\n 'All authorized trajectories shown were successful executions. No failed or abandoned trial receipt is present in this scoped input; no missing failure or old campaign result is invented.'\n ]},\n 'reproduction':{'entry_source_sha256':hist[parent]['source_sha256'],'entry_source_verified':True,'ancestor_sources_all_match_workspace_hashes':True,'data_identity':ctx['protocol']['data_identity'],'dataset_revision':ctx['protocol']['dataset_revision'],'raw_data_access':'Not supplied in proposal jail; cannot freshly verify released parquet digests or execute loader. Inherit host-frozen identity, require host prerequisites rather than inventing a local data audit.','execution':'Host loads each standalone file with its literal CONFIG/variant config, frozen protocol and seed. Use authorized host interface only; no training command is supplied in this jail.','selection':'Validation four-task macro AUC, then macro Logloss, parameters and trial ID. Compare every source and all controls. No per-task veto. No holdout access.'},\n 'validation_plan':{\n 'local_completed':['AST syntax and compile checks for all four modules','All imports allowed; no candidate filesystem/network operations','Exact incumbent replay SHA256 matches the committed source','All three replacement modules identical outside literal CONFIG','Parameter, buffer and explicit initialization construction calls match incumbent in order','25 incumbent methods unchanged; only pool_values, retrieval initializer/forward, and Model initializer/forward edited','New flags read from literal CONFIG; all frozen host parameters absent from configs'],\n 'host_required_before_training':['Finite frozen-BF16 forward, four probability outputs [B,1], sum-four-BCE and backward on empty, zero-length, singleton, full and mixed histories','Same-seed parameter/state_dict equality across new arms and incumbent; no change to inherited CPU RNG or initial g0 predictions, since residual output starts zero','Content/adaptive mode in new common code must match exact incumbent forward and gradients with loaded identical weights, before training; replay must reproduce committed result within documented numerical tolerance','Invalid-padding ID and task-mask perturbation invariance, current-target action invariance, zero/padding-ID no-match checks and null behavior','Uniform weights sum to one over valid history only (null only if empty); mean result independent of task queries and event rank when values and mask fixed','DIN replacement before low-rank maps equals pooled[:,0] expanded over tasks; identity-state replacement equals original token identities times token_valid and cannot see dynamic g0 token content','After a controlled nonzero residual-output perturbation or a host update, verify active value-map gradients, expected zero query gradients in mean/DIN controls, branch-state sensitivity only in adaptive arms, and empty-history residual zero','Measure total and gradient-active parameter counts, full train/inference time, peak GPU memory and four task/slice metrics; do not infer equal effective compute from parameter equality'],\n 'not_completed':'Numerical tests, data execution, new training, new validation, bootstrap and seed repetitions; PyTorch is unavailable and installation/training are prohibited in this workspace.',\n 'uncertainty':'Host-authorized paired seeds and paired user-cluster bootstrap only where available within the remaining budget. No raw user IDs or per-example predictions are available here; do not fabricate bootstrap intervals or infer significance from a single run.'},\n 'assessment_boundary':'Only the prospective proposal and model modules are delivered in this phase. No withheld outcomes read or requested, no human-owned knowledge edited, no disabled personal-memory file created. New observations are recorded with provenance in this proposal for host ingestion; no standalone memory-writing interface is authorized.'\n}\n(p/'proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json:',(p/'proposal.json').stat().st_size,'bytes')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
